<p id="S7.T1.5" class="ltx_p ltx_align_right ltx_figure_panel"><sup id="S7.T1.5.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S7.T1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;">†</span></sup><span id="S7.T1.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> Calibration Data Size   <sup id="S7.T1.5.2.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S7.T1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">‡</span></sup> Learning Rate <span id="S7.T1.5.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom"><span style="visibility:hidden">000</span></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S7.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Supporting Lower Precisions on NPU.</span>
Our custom NPU supports 4/8-bit mixed-precision inference and can be extended to 2-bit computation by splitting each 4-bit MAC into two 2-bit MACs, enabling four parallel 2-bit MACs per 8-bit PE. This extension, however, creates a trade-off between hardware utilization and quantization granularity. Fully utilizing the 32<math id="S7.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>32 systolic array in 2-bit mode requires a minimum channel group size of 128 (32 PEs <math id="S7.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 4 MACs/PE), but grouping so many channels can reduce model accuracy. To mitigate this, spatial PE multiplexing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>)</cite> can partition the PE array to perform 2-bit and 8-bit computation concurrently.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8. </span>Evaluation</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section evaluates the trade-offs between latency and accuracy in deep learning models quantized with FlexiQ. We first describe the evaluation setup and then present the experimental results.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.1. </span>Evaluation Setup</h3>

<figure id="S8.T2" class="ltx_table">

